<h2 id="sites-modules-section-free-abelian-sheaf" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="03CQ">18.5</span> Free abelian sheaves</h2>

<p>
Here is the notion of a free abelian sheaf on a sheaf of sets. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-definition" id="03AA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03AA">Definition <span data-tag="03AA">18.5.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a presheaf of sets. The <em>free abelian sheaf</em> $\mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}^\# $ on $\mathcal{G}$ is the abelian sheaf $\mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}^\# $ which is the sheafification of the free abelian presheaf on $\mathcal{G}$. In the special case $\mathcal{G} = h_ X$ of a representable presheaf associated to an object $X$ of $\mathcal{C}$ we use the notation $\mathbf{Z}_ X^\# $. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<p>
This construction is clearly functorial in the presheaf $\mathcal{G}$. In fact it provides an adjoint to the forgetful functor $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. Here is the precise statement. 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="03AB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03AB">Lemma <span data-tag="03AB">18.5.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{G}$, $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaves of sets. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian sheaf. Let $U$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \begin{align*}  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})}(h_ U^\# , \mathcal{F}) &  = \mathcal{F}(U), \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C})}(\mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}^\# , \mathcal{A}) &  = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})}(\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{A}), \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{C})}(\mathbf{Z}_ U^\# , \mathcal{A}) &  = \mathcal{A}(U). \end{align*}
</div>
  <p> All of these equalities are functorial. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
<p>
<article class="env-lemma" id="03AC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03AC">Lemma <span data-tag="03AC">18.5.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a presheaf of sets. Then $\mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}^\#  = (\mathbf{Z}_{\mathcal{G}^\# })^\# $. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
